I don't quite like that monster-change part of the proposal. My view
e.g. of elementals is that they are powerful beings that are (in case
of the fire elemental) inherently fiery, there's no substrate to
extinguish, they are not burning, rather they *are* the fire; no plain
snow should do them any harm (even if we would introduce some
all-problem-solving-Magic-Snow explanation to legitimate such a design
I wouldn't like it). Similarly with demons or devils, and given the
literary charater (or the one depicted in the film) I wouldn't expect
a balrog to be affected at all by snow.

Hitting an elemental with an artifact, deliberately designed as being
magic, is another case; giving some damage bonus against complementary
elementals is fine, IMO.

Janis

